    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177-a1">

                <pb facs="0361" n="233" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg233"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Garland to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 11,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send you, for your
                    information, a copy of a letter of the 10th instant from United States Attorney
                    Root, New York, in relation to the steamer Albano, which cleared that morning
                    for a port in the United States of Colombia, having arms upon her manifest. I
                    respectfully call your attention to the request of the attorney that he may
                    receive, at the earliest possible moment, such further and more particular
                    information as the minister of the United States of Colombia maybe able to give,
                    and shall be pleased to receive such information as the Department of State may
                    be able to furnish, that I may transmit it promptly to the attorney.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. H. GARLAND,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Attorney-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
